{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror","id":1462410,"title":"Family and Magick, Risk and Personal Horror","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-02T01:43:33-07:00","id":1462410,"title":"Family and Magick, Risk and Personal Horror","content":"I previously did a post, before Technocracy Reloaded dropped, about the possibility of Elite Boarding Schools for Technomancers' Neglected Kids: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1422565-elite-boarding-schools-for-technomancers-neglected-kids\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...neglected-kids</a><br /> <br /> This is mainly focused on the Traditions who I imagine as having a closer connection to their sleeper families than career driven Technomancers in a high demand bureaucracy. Some basic questions:<br /> <br /> - What is marriage on a metaphysical and spiritual level?<br /> <br /> - Is there Magick that you can do if you are married that you couldn't do if you weren't?<br /> <br /> - Would Mages always prefer to have the companionship of another Mage who understands Magick over a sleeper who doesn't?<br /> <br /> - Do children raised by Mages have an increased chance to Awaken?<br /> <br /> I have given some thought to the possibility of Tradition Mages with sleeper families using their close connection to them as a conduit for Magick intended to influence the local community and larger society. You would obviously want to strengthen and empower family members before using them as conduits. In game terms, they might be considered Acolytes or Assistants who could aide in High Ritual. They might also act as messengers, communicating the effects of Mind Magick by proxy, with perhaps a little Correspondence or Life. They may be unknowing participants.<br /> <br /> There are two firm stances that someone could take on the choice of whether or not to involve family members in casting Magick and spreading one's influence:<br /> <br /> A) Using family to facilitate Magick in the context of the Ascension War is wrong, because it endangers them by making them potential targets.<br /> <br /> B) The mere fact that you are a Tradition Mage makes your family members targets, regardless of the choice. By involving them, you can empower them with Magick and help them prepare for what they might face. If they are unaware of their role in the diffusion of Magick, the Magick is already subtle enough to avoid enemy detection.<br /> <br /> Things stay interesting if we assume that some PCs and NPCs will chose B:<br /> <br /> - What are some effects that you would cast on or using members of your family?<br /> <br /> - What kind of businesses could a Mage's family get involved in that best suit the goals of the Mage or their Tradition?<br /> <br /> - What is the ideal way for this to turn out?<br /> <br /> - What is the worst that could happen to a family member as a result of their involvement, knowing or unknowing? - Curses, death, abduction, imprisonment? - A miscast spell that was intended to be beneficial?<br /> <br /> - And, of course, the personal horror aspect - How is the Mage impacted by harm to their family as a result of their choice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 10-03-2021, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T07:20:50-07:00","id":1462422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror#post1462410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Would Mages always prefer to have the companionship of another Mage who understands Magick over a sleeper who doesn't?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just from reading the books (mostly Traditions' books, from what I remember) it seems to me that relations (whether marriage or not) are much more often between Mages than between a Mage and a mundane human. On the other hand, this might be because of the focus on detailing the lives of Mages in the books; mundane humans are rarely mentioned.<br /> The Verbenae are keen on maintaining families under their purview, and I guess most of them cannot be formed from Mage to Mage marriages.<br /> <br /> I think that most Mages would be more attracted and would find forming a relation easier with another Mage. Would most Mages abandon their mundane partner if a relationship with another Mage would seem possible? Not necessarily. But I think that quite many would at least consider it. A mundane human has relatively little to offer that is comparable to a Mage's perspectives, the politics of Mages, the joy of casting Magick, the Ascension War, a Paradigm etc. Though I also believe in the power of love and the meaningfulness of a formed relation and shared experiences; this would definitely be something to hold on to in relations between a Mage and a mundane human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-02-2021, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T18:55:39-07:00","id":1462503,"title":"","content":"Even if not marrying another Mage, one would be more likely to marry a Sleeper follower of their Tradition (I always forget the name of those). Someone that is still fairly involved in the world of magic and probably on board with the Mage's Paradigm. And as people that deal with the most awesome extremes of the world, Mages are generally also more prone to have relationships to exceptional people, like members of other major or minor supernatural splats, witnesses of magic that manage to remember and somewhat understand what they saw, time travelers...<br /> <br /> So those relationships carry the answer with themselves. They are already profoundly touched by the supernatural and will work based on their specific experiences.<br /> <br /> A truly common marriage is possible, but unlikely. If it happens, then the Mage is is prone to either slowly bring their loved ones to the supernatural world, or become ever more stranded from this family as they delve in a world they can't even share with a spouse, or yet do this to their own Avatar and favor marriage instead of magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T21:50:26-07:00","id":1462512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462503#post1462503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if not marrying another Mage, one would be more likely to marry a Sleeper follower of their Tradition (I always forget the name of those).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure it's Acolyte.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462503#post1462503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone that is still fairly involved in the world of magic and probably on board with the Mage's Paradigm. And as people that deal with the most awesome extremes of the world, Mages are generally also more prone to have relationships to exceptional people, like members of other major or minor supernatural splats, witnesses of magic that manage to remember and somewhat understand what they saw, time travelers...<br /> <br /> So those relationships carry the answer with themselves. They are already profoundly touched by the supernatural and will work based on their specific experiences.<br /> <br /> A truly common marriage is possible, but unlikely. If it happens, then the Mage is is prone to either slowly bring their loved ones to the supernatural world, or become ever more stranded from this family as they delve in a world they can't even share with a spouse, or yet do this to their own Avatar and favor marriage instead of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>A funny thing just occurred to me. I don't use the Avatar Storm Metaplot, because I like the open ended possibilities of being able to explore the Umbra. A lot of people do use it and sight the reason developers explained; that they wanted to force Mages and the players who play them to focus on Earth, sleepers and terrestrial concerns. I'm not concluding that you and @Maud'Dib are a representative sample of Mage players on OPF, but the fact that the first two replies state the view that Mages would tend to avoid marriage with sleepers is... interesting, let's say.<br /> <br /> Vampire and Werewolf set the tone for WoD, focusing on horror and degeneration. Mage has this element, but you are more free to chose a path that avoids disconnection from the rest of humanity. Being married to a sleeper, who you have the option of making an Acolyte, is something that anchors you in the sleeper community that surrounds you. If it turns that the majority of Mage players would be of the opinion that Mages would rarely or almost never marry sleepers, then it leaves me to wonder why people would discard the richness of the Umbra in the name of grounding the game in the concerns of sleepers in their day to day lives. I find myself in the odd position - not an uncomfortable one, just a bit funny.<br /> <br /> I write NPC Mages who are married to sleepers, working Magick through familial connection. My own character is engaged to a sleeper character, the daughter of a powerful Mage from a different Tradition than his own. At the same time, I'm brewing adventures set far away in unknown depths. And certainly, the idea that Mages would gravitate toward each other factors into my thinking. One has to consider all the conflicting pressures on individual Mages alone, their Avatar and Mentor making conflicting demands, Cabal and Chantry Politics. When you put two Mages with all these pressures acting on them in a long term relationship, it can be as epic as it is chaotic. If Mages are mostly a private sex club amongst each other, one that excludes sleepers, then they are acting like a class that wants nothing to do with an inferior class, except to tell the inferior class what they should believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T22:35:38-07:00","id":1462515,"title":"","content":"Be attentive that I didn't said a Mage wouldn't marry a Sleeper. I said they would marry a Sleeper in the know. I don't think at all that most Mages marry among themselves.<br /> <br /> The thing is how marriages work. Relationships in general work on some sort of common ground. You don't just know the person, but you two have some common context and experiences. Things you talk about, things you have either a common understanding or a clear disagreement, there are things that affect both of you. On any relationship there are common elements between your lives. And the less such elements a relationship have, the more you grow apart.<br /> <br /> Familial relationships have a lot of those naturally, as the family itself is unavoidable common ground for many of its members, but there is an exception: the couple. Their common ground isn't innate, they <b>can</b> grow apart. They can part ways or have a strained relationship, or even become so distant from each other that this can barely be called a marriage anymore.<br /> <br /> What it means to be married to someone you have nothing in common, you don't even understand their life and possibly know next to nothing about?<br /> <br /> If the Mage makes their spouse into an Acolyte, then no problem. It is even possible that many Mages would prefer this to a relationship to another Mage even if this Acolyte isn't actually on to their Paradigm, but at least understand the world the Mage lives in. If the Mage spends more time with mundane activities and work, so the bulk of their lives is mundane and can be shared with their spouse, also no problem, but this Mage is distancing from Mage society.<br /> <br /> A dedicated Mage, though, that marries to a common Sleeper, will have a spouse with whom they can't talk about anything of a big chunk of their life. To whom they can't show their greatest achievements. With whom they can't commemorate important victories by what they are. They can build pretenses and false explanations, but what does this lack of fellowship does for their feelings towards that person?<br /> <br /> Marriage is a big thing. It is partnership and compromise. People coming together to share their lives and destinies. It may be out of love or any other reason, but they are still in that together like it or not. When you're not in that together anymore, can you call this a marriage?<br /> <br /> Just to be clear: a character keeps secrets but still spends a lot of time with their family still have this. The trope of the spouse that is secretly whatever else holds because this character is still present most of the time and emotionally invested in their family. OR precisely getting stranded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T09:40:09-07:00","id":1462561,"title":"","content":"Something else to consider: Mages are willful. It is inherent in what they do. On average, sleepers aren't quite so willful. There are exceptions, of course; but as a rule, Mages will be willful while sleepers won't be.One effect of this is that an ideological class between two Mages is going to be a much bigger deal than an ideological class between a Mage and a Sleeper. So the success of a marriage between two Mages is far more likely to be dependent on the compatibility of their Foci then a marriage between a Mage and a Sleeper. <br /> <br /> But I would hesitate to generalize about who Mages are likely to marry. Marriage is an intensely personal thing, and will probably depend on factors other than stuff about Magick. I suspect that Mages are likely to choose marriage partners in much the same way that everyone else does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T13:00:12-07:00","id":1462580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462515#post1462515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Be attentive that I didn't said a Mage wouldn't marry a Sleeper. I said they would marry a Sleeper in the know. I don't think at all that most Mages marry among themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462515#post1462515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is how marriages work. Relationships in general work on some sort of common ground. You don't just know the person, but you two have some common context and experiences. Things you talk about, things you have either a common understanding or a clear disagreement, there are things that affect both of you. On any relationship there are common elements between your lives. And the less such elements a relationship have, the more you grow apart.<br /> <br /> Familial relationships have a lot of those naturally, as the family itself is unavoidable common ground for many of its members, but there is an exception: the couple. Their common ground isn't innate, they <b>can</b> grow apart. They can part ways or have a strained relationship, or even become so distant from each other that this can barely be called a marriage anymore.<br /> <br /> What it means to be married to someone you have nothing in common, you don't even understand their life and possibly know next to nothing about?</div> </div> </div> </div>The common ground might just be mutual sexual attraction. It's often the case that people whose personalities and interests don't suit each other live together in a fight-ridden long-term relationship (which my government calls a common law marriage). They fight and fuck. And it can be a lack of fighting that causes a couple to grow apart, because neither party has had a chance to firmly state their positions. Perfect harmony can be a relationship-killer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462515#post1462515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Mage makes their spouse into an Acolyte, then no problem. It is even possible that many Mages would prefer this to a relationship to another Mage even if this Acolyte isn't actually on to their Paradigm, but at least understand the world the Mage lives in. If the Mage spends more time with mundane activities and work, so the bulk of their lives is mundane and can be shared with their spouse, also no problem, but this Mage is distancing from Mage society.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did a post on &quot;Effect of Awakening on who you are Attracted to&quot; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1423165-effect-of-awakening-on-who-you-are-attracted-to\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-attracted-to</a><br /> Distancing yourself from Mage Society can be good for survival and longevity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462515#post1462515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A dedicated Mage, though, that marries to a common Sleeper, will have a spouse with whom they can't talk about anything of a big chunk of their life. To whom they can't show their greatest achievements. With whom they can't commemorate important victories by what they are. They can build pretenses and false explanations, but what does this lack of fellowship does for their feelings towards that person?</div> </div> </div> </div>As difficult as this might be, I think it would often be the case. My Mage-to-sleeper-ratio is 1 per 100,000 and this would be considered high compared to what one of the hosts on Mage The Podcast stated, 1 per 500,000 (I put an even higher concentration where the plot happens). Most Newly Awakened Mages don't immediately rise above their biologically hardwired lust, even if they can see more deeply into people. The statistical odds that the first group of Mages they meet is going to consist of at least one person they are more sexually attracted to than the most attractive sleeper of the sex they prefer in their city is going to be low. Their newfound abilities improve their odds of going for that beautiful sleeper they could only have dreamed about pre-Awakening. Romantic love and sexual attraction are not separate things. They overlap to a great degree. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462515#post1462515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Marriage is a big thing. It is partnership and compromise. People coming together to share their lives and destinies. It may be out of love or any other reason, but they are still in that together like it or not. When you're not in that together anymore, can you call this a marriage?</div> </div> </div> </div>The sleeper spouse who is being pulled toward becoming an Acolyte is making a huge compromise. They are being asked to unlearn things they thought true that allowed them to navigate life and survive - and without any high likelihood of being able to learn true Magick themselves. You could very loosely compare Awakened versus sleeper to high IQ versus low IQ. Advantageous partnerships are often between people of widely different IQs and other traits, each benefiting from their spouse's advantage in an area in which they are not particularly advantaged.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462515#post1462515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to be clear: a character keeps secrets but still spends a lot of time with their family still have this. The trope of the spouse that is secretly whatever else holds because this character is still present most of the time and emotionally invested in their family. OR precisely getting stranded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both very true. That's what makes the story interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462561#post1462561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something else to consider: Mages are willful. It is inherent in what they do. On average, sleepers aren't quite so willful. There are exceptions, of course; but as a rule, Mages will be willful while sleepers won't be.</div> </div> </div> </div>And people are selfish. A Mage might prefer an attractive and malleable mate who supports them while they concentrate on metaphysical mysteries. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462561#post1462561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One effect of this is that an ideological class between two Mages is going to be a much bigger deal than an ideological class between a Mage and a Sleeper. So the success of a marriage between two Mages is far more likely to be dependent on the compatibility of their Foci then a marriage between a Mage and a Sleeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Put that laptop down. You look like a Technomancer! I won't be caught dead at the power circle with you lugging that around.&quot; (sigh) &quot;I have an extra wand. Here. Now we're late. Let's go.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462561#post1462561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I would hesitate to generalize about who Mages are likely to marry. Marriage is an intensely personal thing, and will probably depend on factors other than stuff about Magick. I suspect that Mages are likely to choose marriage partners in much the same way that everyone else does.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect (and in my experience) most players create Mage characters who are single at the time of Awakening to facilitate the high-demand commitment to membership in a Cabal or a Symposium. But, I think a storyteller necessarily generalizes to some degree when they populate their setting with NPCs who are unmarried, uncommitted, polyamorous or married to either a Mage or sleeper. It is going to average out to some kind of generalized view. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T13:08:24-07:00","id":1462581,"title":"","content":"Only if they have a generalized view of mages. A Chorister is going to have a very different view on marriage than a Cultist; and who knows what an Etherite thinks about it? <br /> <br /> My point is that Mages are about as far from being homogeneous as you can get. So trying to State some sort of General rule about, well, just about <i>anything</i> verges on the pointless. It's like asking about the average <i>human's</i> view on marriage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T13:53:03-07:00","id":1462588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror#post1462410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- What is marriage on a metaphysical and spiritual level?</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, that's something the mage has to think about. What is marriage for your gods, or your science!, or your philosophy? It may be a deep mystical bond, or just a social convention. It migth even be an obstacle in the path, for the more asceticaly inclined.<br /> <br /> As <i>Dataweaver </i>says, mages are a varied lot. There's not a general answer, but many answers. More so in the Traditions or Disparate, that have many very different cosmologies within.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Is there Magick that you can do if you are married that you couldn't do if you weren't? </div> </div> </div>No. Well, maybe.<br /> <br /> There's no actual RAW advantage, but a mage that has a Focus based on vows or community could have &quot;marriage as a Focus&quot;, so to speak (like, a wedding can be seen as a ritual). Again, that depend on your Focus - and that's sopmething the player decides. It may well be that a player want's marriage to have a metaphisical load for their character, and I would allow it as per normal Focus rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Would Mages always prefer to have the companionship of another Mage who understands Magick over a sleeper who doesn't? </div> </div> </div>No, I don't think so.<br /> <br /> I don't even think it's a matter of Focus. People can get married to people who have different sets of beliefs. This may/will cause friction, but real life relationships often have friction.<br /> <br /> Your &quot;second life&quot; as a mage, however, would be much more of a hurdle - in many, many ways. As has been explored by the posts above. It would be better for the relationship if they understand what you are and what you do, and that ain't easy when you're a person whose desired lifestyle defies what people considers not just normal, but <i>real</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Do children raised by Mages have an increased chance to Awaken? </div> </div> </div>It's unknown.<br /> <br /> As I see it, Awakening it's a kind of breaktrough where you see Reality it's not what you've been tought it is, and that you can interact with a deeper layer of metaphisics that allow you to master reality (Reality &gt; reality). But I think if you're raised in a &quot;magical&quot; environment, that may as well be the hurdle you need to overcome.You need something to rock those principles to Awaken<br /> <br /> Or maybe not. Maybe the technocratical, static, and mundane, reality it's to blame for the small amount of mages. Perhaps in a more magical (wonderous) world, children would have an easier time Awakening (or never go to sleep in the first place, as per the book that suggests all children are born Awake)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are two firm stances that someone could take on the choice of whether or not to involve family members in casting Magick and spreading one's influence:<br /> <br /> A) Using family to facilitate Magick in the context of the Ascension War is wrong, because it endangers them by making them potential targets. </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting point, because involving sleepers in the Ascencion War it's against the general code of the Traditions. At the very least, it would be considered unethical. At worst, it could be punisheable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> B) The mere fact that you are a Tradition Mage makes your family members targets, regardless of the choice. By involving them, you can empower them with Magick and help them prepare for what they might face. If they are unaware of their role in the diffusion of Magick, the Magick is already subtle enough to avoid enemy detection. </div> </div> </div>But this is a thing.<br /> <br /> For A) and B) I think that your previous post of &quot;magical boarding schools&quot; provides a good context. The Ascencion War it's vicious enough that technocrats are encouraged to leave aside their personal ties, and it wouldn't be out of character to consider putting their children on a higly secure boarding school for protection<br /> <br /> Well, Technocrats are the wining faction, the most powerful Mage organization. Targeting the human family of a Technocrat isn't just unethical (And a violation of the law of the Traditions about not involving sleepers because &quot;they must be protected, they don't know what they're doing&quot;), it's also opening your people to vicious retaliation by an enemy that *it's* on a better position than you are, and most likely *can* make you pay. Some Traditionalists would do it anyway, but most Traditionalists preffer to lay low instead.<br /> <br /> That's not the same for Technocrats.<br /> 1\u00b0 personal morals aside, the Technocracy hasn't explicit laws against harming individual sleepers. In the Lore, a common image of the Pogrom it's Technocrats killing the family/friends of Traditionalists and replacing them with clones (loyal to the technocracy)<br /> 2\u00b0 A Traditionalist would want to get vengance after having their family killed/replaced, but the Traditions have much less power to retaliate. Technocrats have a higher expectation to end impune after doing this. Heck, it may be done on purpose to try to lure a potentially dangerous mage into a more direct conflict (ofc, this can backfire).<br /> <br /> So, all the concerns that you tought out in that previous thread are <i>worse </i>for the Traditions.<br /> <br /> Traditionalist can sometimes be seen like a guerrilla. In these cases it's <i>really, really, much better</i> to cut all emotional relationship with everyone, unless they're in deep waters like you are (Acolites). This is the most common scenario (and if this clashes with Revised stance on more &quot;humane&quot; mages...well, no wonder.). This is the most basic interpretation of the Laws of the Traditions that involve sleepers (the one about protecting them, and the rule of shade - put together)<br /> <br /> BUT because mages are humane, weren't typically born from a cabbage, and will like people that aren't mages...I think B) it's reasonable and understandable, it stands to reason that a mage would use magick to protect their loved ones regardless of their knowledge of the magical world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - What are some effects that you would cast on or using members of your family? </div> </div> </div>From the top of my head:<br /> Corr can let you sense where they are (and how with other Spheres).<br /> Give them a Wonder that allows teleportation to a safe place<br /> Bless them with some form of good luck<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - What kind of businesses could a Mage's family get involved in that best suit the goals of the Mage or their Tradition? </div> </div> </div>A mage would want them to be involved in whatever activities the mage believes are good and right - usually these align with these goals in the mage's head<br /> <br /> From a more pragmatic perspective, if they want to help with the &quot;good fight&quot;: Business that would provide monetary resources, and/or valuable contacts that mages may be to bussy to develop and sustain by themselves?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - What is the ideal way for this to turn out? </div> </div> </div>You and your family will defeat the Technocracy and live happy ever after?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - What is the worst that could happen to a family member as a result of their involvement, knowing or unknowing? - Curses, death, abduction, imprisonment? </div> </div> </div>Yes<br /> <br /> Also brainwashing, haunting by spirits, exposure to eldrich madness, becoming lost in the other worlds, having their souls offered to a demon...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A miscast spell that was intended to be beneficial? </div> </div> </div>Usually these hurt the mage more than the target. A possible exception could be a Wonder that has a side effect.<br /> <br /> Also, a spell that could be benefitial has the potential to be problematic if the mage didn't read the situation well enough or wasn't careful. Like, maybe you place so many Wards against everything arround their house that it ends blipping a bit too hard in NWO magick radars, and thus you end placing your family in more danger then they needed to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - And, of course, the personal horror aspect - How is the Mage impacted by harm to their family as a result of their choice? </div> </div> </div>Typically, as any human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-03-2021, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T18:12:19-07:00","id":1462600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462588#post1462588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, that's something the mage has to think about. What is marriage for your gods, or your science!, or your philosophy? It may be a deep mystical bond, or just a social convention. It migth even be an obstacle in the path, for the more asceticaly inclined.<br /> <br /> As <i>Dataweaver </i>says, mages are a varied lot. There's not a general answer, but many answers. More so in the Traditions or Disparate, that have many very different cosmologies within.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a Mage believes they are on a Personal path toward Transcendence, they must necessarily consider leaving any spouse they have behind. Since A LOT of Mages pursue Personal Ascension, I think this affects Mages' views on marriage. At the same time, the goal of uplifting humanity toward a Collective Ascension might place high value on marriage as a necessary component of the process. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462588#post1462588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. Well, maybe.<br /> <br /> There's no actual RAW advantage, but a mage that has a Focus based on vows or community could have &quot;marriage as a Focus&quot;, so to speak (like, a wedding can be seen as a ritual). Again, that depend on your Focus - and that's sopmething the player decides. It may well be that a player want's marriage to have a metaphisical load for their character, and I would allow it as per normal Focus rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can certainly apply to and facilitate the development of Devotional Resonance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462588#post1462588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I don't think so.<br /> <br /> I don't even think it's a matter of Focus. People can get married to people who have different sets of beliefs. This may/will cause friction, but real life relationships often have friction.<br /> <br /> Your &quot;second life&quot; as a mage, however, would be much more of a hurdle - in many, many ways. As has been explored by the posts above. It would be better for the relationship if they understand what you are and what you do, and that ain't easy when you're a person whose desired lifestyle defies what people considers not just normal, but <i>real</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>A NWO Watcher might program an AI to scour the Internet for sleepers posting worried questions on mental health forums about claims made by a Mage-spouse while trying to turn them into an Acolyte.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462588#post1462588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's unknown.<br /> <br /> As I see it, Awakening it's a kind of breaktrough where you see Reality it's not what you've been tought it is, and that you can interact with a deeper layer of metaphisics that allow you to master reality (Reality &gt; reality). But I think if you're raised in a &quot;magical&quot; environment, that may as well be the hurdle you need to overcome.You need something to rock those principles to Awaken<br /> <br /> Or maybe not. Maybe the technocratical, static, and mundane, reality it's to blame for the small amount of mages. Perhaps in a more magical (wonderous) world, children would have an easier time Awakening (or never go to sleep in the first place, as per the book that suggests all children are born Awake)</div> </div> </div> </div>A strict Traditionalist parent could try too hard and cause an adolescent rebellion where the teenage kid gravitates toward the Technocracy, perhaps as an Extraordinary Citizen and not a Mage. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462588#post1462588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an interesting point, because involving sleepers in the Ascencion War it's against the general code of the Traditions. At the very least, it would be considered unethical. At worst, it could be punisheable.</div> </div> </div> </div>In an extreme case, an Order of Hermes Mage who long ago detached himself from sleeper society to become a Chantry-higherup might hand down punishment to an initiate Mage simply for having a family.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462588#post1462588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this is a thing.<br /> <br /> For A) and B) I think that your previous post of &quot;magical boarding schools&quot; provides a good context. The Ascencion War it's vicious enough that technocrats are encouraged to leave aside their personal ties, and it wouldn't be out of character to consider putting their children on a higly secure boarding school for protection<br /> <br /> Well, Technocrats are the wining faction, the most powerful Mage organization. Targeting the human family of a Technocrat isn't just unethical (And a violation of the law of the Traditions about not involving sleepers because &quot;they must be protected, they don't know what they're doing&quot;), it's also opening your people to vicious retaliation by an enemy that *it's* on a better position than you are, and most likely *can* make you pay. Some Traditionalists would do it anyway, but most Traditionalists preffer to lay low instead.<br /> <br /> That's not the same for Technocrats.<br /> 1\u00b0 personal morals aside, the Technocracy hasn't explicit laws against harming individual sleepers. In the Lore, a common image of the Pogrom it's Technocrats killing the family/friends of Traditionalists and replacing them with clones (loyal to the technocracy)<br /> 2\u00b0 A Traditionalist would want to get vengance after having their family killed/replaced, but the Traditions have much less power to retaliate. Technocrats have a higher expectation to end impune after doing this. Heck, it may be done on purpose to try to lure a potentially dangerous mage into a more direct conflict (ofc, this can backfire).<br /> <br /> So, all the concerns that you tought out in that previous thread are <i>worse </i>for the Traditions.<br /> <br /> Traditionalist can sometimes be seen like a guerrilla. In these cases it's <i>really, really, much better</i> to cut all emotional relationship with everyone, unless they're in deep waters like you are (Acolites). This is the most common scenario (and if this clashes with Revised stance on more &quot;humane&quot; mages...well, no wonder.). This is the most basic interpretation of the Laws of the Traditions that involve sleepers (the one about protecting them, and the rule of shade - put together)<br /> <br /> BUT because mages are humane, weren't typically born from a cabbage, and will like people that aren't mages...I think B) it's reasonable and understandable, it stands to reason that a mage would use magick to protect their loved ones regardless of their knowledge of the magical world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think killing a Mage's family and then using multiple Prime2, Life 5, Mind5 effects to replace them with clones loyal to the Technocracy would be a decision motivated by sadism rather than strategic considerations. The larger an organization becomes, the more wasteful it tends to get. Syndicate - Disbursements would have some opinion. The Traditionalist might simply communicate with Disbursements, explaining that he is still alive after FACADE used untold funds only to leave behind evidence of genetic fuckery as the clones break down. Let the audit come down before starting the rest of his planned vendetta. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462588#post1462588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the top of my head:<br /> Corr can let you sense where they are (and how with other Spheres).<br /> Give them a Wonder that allows teleportation to a safe place<br /> Bless them with some form of good luck</div> </div> </div> </div>This would hopefully prevent the protected loved one from killed by an enemy that has no qualms about killing and cloning. Luck let's them survive long enough for the caster to sense the danger and teleport to the scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462588#post1462588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mage would want them to be involved in whatever activities the mage believes are good and right - usually these align with these goals in the mage's head<br /> <br /> From a more pragmatic perspective, if they want to help with the &quot;good fight&quot;: Business that would provide monetary resources, and/or valuable contacts that mages may be to bussy to develop and sustain by themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>In my Chronicle, it's a Verbena marrying into a family involved in the lumber industry to control how the company operates. The intimate closeness of marriage is needed to supplant the Syndicate's formerly established influence. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462588#post1462588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You and your family will defeat the Technocracy and live happy ever after?</div> </div> </div> </div>I need to rethink that question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462588#post1462588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes<br /> <br /> Also brainwashing, haunting by spirits, exposure to eldrich madness, becoming lost in the other worlds, having their souls offered to a demon...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Nephandi! I hadn't factored them into this exploration of Mages and their families. Might as well include Marauders, the earlier versions of which were criticized for bearing no resemblance to any real mental health diagnosis, often hereditary. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462588#post1462588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Usually these hurt the mage more than the target. A possible exception could be a Wonder that has a side effect.<br /> <br /> Also, a spell that could be benefitial has the potential to be problematic if the mage didn't read the situation well enough or wasn't careful. Like, maybe you place so many Wards against everything arround their house that it ends blipping a bit too hard in NWO magick radars, and thus you end placing your family in more danger then they needed to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a player botch a Life role. The teenage character was trying to make her father tired so he would go to sleep, allowing her to sneak out. It ended up in a trip to the hospital with some meaningful dialogue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462588#post1462588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Typically, as any human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trauma, for Mages, includes the possibility of Quiet - usually Madness, now that I'm considering Outsiders.<br /> <br /> Thanks for taking the time to answer each question.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T20:50:57-07:00","id":1462608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462580#post1462580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The common ground might just be mutual sexual attraction.</div> </div> </div> </div>A couple that only fight and fuck have more than a single common ground, as they have reasons to fight. Common ground isn't the same as things both like, it can be even something negative in their relationship. People with strong opinions about one thing have common ground even if their opinions are opposite. People that hate each other have common ground. If two people stay in the same house for hours every day, sharing that space and its events regularly, they have common ground. The opposite of common ground is absence, being absent from one's life for a big chunk of it.<br /> <br /> Sex can start a relationship, but it won't be the only thing in the relationship for long, otherwise there won't be a relationship for long.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462580#post1462580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As difficult as this might be, I think it would often be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again you forget that I'm talking about marrying common Sleepers (and keeping them that way), not any Sleeper. An Acolyte is a pretty sufficient compromise for the relationship to work. Now this person <b>does</b> understand your world even if they can't grasp how you do things. Now you can share with them, or fight over magic-related stuff with them. Even if this is a bad relationship, it does have common ground, although it can be good, of course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462580#post1462580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sleeper spouse who is being pulled toward becoming an Acolyte is making a huge compromise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I even said that I would think a relationship between Mage and Acolyte more common than Mage and Mage (or Mage and Vampire, Mage and Werewolf, Mage and Ghoul, Mage and Kinfolk, Mage and Changeling, Mage and Kinain... all relationships with good opportunities for building common ground).<br /> <br /> One thing I must make clear is the role of common ground here. It is not about building a good relationship or having good emotions. It is about having emotional attachment at all. Without common ground couples grow apart because their feelings naturally change and weaken. Human emotions are dynamic, unending love, by itself, is just romantic bullshit. If there is nothing keeping the emotional weight and investment in place, feelings die. Relationships can be sustained by bad feelings (although it isn't a good thing, obviously), but not in an emotional void. They'll become strangers to each other and that's all.<br /> <br /> Common ground exists even in an extremely unequal or abusive relationship. A mage that wants a malleable companion quickly becomes the most important thing in this other person's life by shaping it, while the Mage devotes some time to shape this life for the other and have a trusted servitor. This is common ground. They share something, even if not from an equal standpoint. Even if for the Mage most of this is more a pet project than commitment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T06:23:21-07:00","id":1462646,"title":"","content":"This thread reminds me of this scene from Gravity Falls :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xxuqXE399hg\" data-code=\"xxuqXE399hg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/xxuqXE399hg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T21:16:20-07:00","id":1463538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1462410-family-and-magick-risk-and-personal-horror?p=1462588#post1462588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, a spell that could be benefitial has the potential to be problematic if the mage didn't read the situation well enough or wasn't careful. Like, maybe you place so many Wards against everything arround their house that it ends blipping a bit too hard in NWO magick radars, and thus you end placing your family in more danger then they needed to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something I thought about when it comes to using magick to protect a loved one. The very act of doing so makes them potentially a target for those with the ability to sense the interference. Whether it's Prime mages who can sense spells themselves, or any mage whose understanding of Spheres allows them to know when those Spheres have been twisted around someone. Anyone with Entropy could see if someone has been blessed with good luck.<br /> <br /> Now, what that party does with this knowledge can vary. Any Sorcerer with dots in Fortune can make someone luckier. How often does any given mage investigate random people who might just have a little magical help or a good luck charm? But at the very least, if someone is walking around with enchantments on them, that might get someone's attention. Which could lead to all sorts of trouble.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, the best thing a mage can do for their loved ones is to keep them indistinguishable from every other random person.<br /> <br /> Not that mages are above falling to temptation. When you have the power to warp reality, it can be so easy to try to make life easier or safer for the ones you love, through the most direct means available.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another thing is that using magick to interfere can gain the attention of anyone, even if they can't sense magic, if the effects of that interference affects someone else. If a person gets a promotion because their Awakened spouse nudged things in their favor, it might create resentment among those who got passed over for promotion. Granted, this could happen regardless of the mage's influence, as being envious or resentful of someone else's good fortune is hardly unique to the supernatural world. But if the professional rival thinks the spouse didn't &quot;earn&quot; their place - or even has reason to suspect the promotion was unusual - they might become suspicious and nosy.<br /> <br /> Their involvement might even be a fluke, the rival reading into things rather than having real evidence (in essence, being right for the wrong reasons). What matters is that manipulating events as the mage did created unintended side effects. The mage is unlikely to stop interfering if they believe their spouse is under threat, even from a mundane enemy. Especially if the rival making a big deal about the matter draws in other parties who are even more dangerous. There are a lot of ways a seemingly small situation could spiral out of a control and become very large, when magick is involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}